t`.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-99-`score` and `bestActiveSessionStreak` copy the committed score-event ledger.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-117-run/completion ID and completion timestamp. Later tutorial completions may add\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-118-their own immutable history/result once, but cannot replace those provenance\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-119-fields or create another milestone. Reopen, restart, failed UI acknowledgement,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:120:and recovery replay are reads unless they initiate a new run.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-121-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-122-### Result and lifecycle fixtures\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-123-\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-125-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-126-| `RESULT-FX-01` | Complete a standard 10-card run, then reopen using its run/completion ID. | One `completed_result`, history entry, and score ledger are stored; reopen returns them without any duplicate completion or milestone. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-127-| `RESULT-FX-02` | Complete `tutorial-v1` TUT-05, then repeat completion after restart with the same IDs. | Exactly one result/history entry and one profile `first_whistle_complete` presence state; retry returns both unchanged. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:128:| `RESULT-FX-03` | Explicitly abandon after card 4, restart, and open its result. | One `abandoned_result`, zero-point abandon event, and no completion milestone; partial score/history is recoverable and no attempt is inferred for card 5. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-129-| `RESULT-FX-04` | Pause at an unresolved card, background/terminate, restart, then resume and complete. | Restore the confirmed unresolved card with no abandon/blank/timeout event; later completion creates one result and eligible tutorial milestone only once. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:130:| `RESULT-FX-05` | On final-card completion, result write is interrupted; restart with a valid prior confirmed snapshot and corrupt draft. | Enter `recovery`, retain snapshot, offer resume-confirmed/discard-draft/return-home; no result or milestone is claimed until a successful completion commits. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-131-| `RESULT-FX-06` | Complete a tutorial, confirm deletion of local history/profile/snapshots, restart, and complete a new tutorial run. | Deletion returns to first launch and removes old local records only after confirmation; the new profile/run can create one new result and one new milestone, with no duplicate residual completion. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-132-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-133-## Release boundary\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-134-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-135-Release validation requires `SCORE-FX-01`\u2013`SCORE-FX-12` and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-136-`RESULT-FX-01`\u2013`RESULT-FX-06`: exactly 18 fixtures. Wrong, blank, enabled\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:137:timeout, and explicit abandon are all recoverable outcomes with a monotonic\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md:138:score and no duplicate completion. Pause, interruption, and recovery are not\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md-139-substitutes for those outcomes and cannot silently manufacture an attempt.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-28-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-29-| Field | Rule / purpose |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-30-| --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:31:| `id`, `revision`, `batchId`, `status` | Stable ID, positive revision, one named batch, and lifecycle: `draft \u2192 fact_checked \u2192 accessibility_edited \u2192 second_reviewed \u2192 published`; alternatively `blocked` or `withdrawn`. Only `published` is eligible. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-32-| `originalityRecord` | Author ID/creation date, independently-authored confirmation, and a non-copying check. It records inspiration boundaries, never reference-product text. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-33-| `promptKey`, `promptText`, `instructionKey` | One independently written, single-fact prompt plus a format-appropriate, plain-language instruction. Prompt text must be answerable without an image, sound, colour, time limit, or unstated context. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-34-| `format` | Exactly one of `four_option_select`, `true_false`, `ordered_pair`, or `short_typed_answer`. |\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-36-| `answerOptions` | Required only for select/true-false. Select has exactly four unique option IDs and one `correct`; true/false has canonical `true`/`false` IDs. Options are text-labelled and have non-colour selection/result states. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-37-| `canonicalAnswer` and `acceptedAnswerRule` | Select/true-false use canonical option IDs; ordered pair specifies exactly two ordered canonical IDs; typed answer provides canonical display answer, normalised accepted aliases, and no fuzzy match. Empty aliases and aliases that could mean another answer are invalid. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-38-| `explanationKey`, `explanationText` | Short fact-first explanation shown after resolution, including canonical answer where useful. It must explain why rather than merely say \"correct\". |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:39:| `accessibility` | `screenReaderPrompt`, `screenReaderOptions` where applicable, `answerStateText`, `explanationTextEquivalent`, reading-order/focus requirement, and text-size/contrast review. No visual or audio-only clue may be needed. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-40-| `provenanceId`, `factualAssertions[]` | Links each assertion to permitted durable sources/research records, source locator, checked date, and conflict/correction history. All assertions must be supported. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:41:| `reviews[]` | Two distinct completed reviews: factual/rights review and accessibility/copy review. Each carries reviewer ID/role, decision, date, findings, and revision reviewed. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:42:| `localeKeys`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `withdrawal` | Externalised player strings and audit timestamps. Withdrawal requires reason, effective date, and replacement relationship only when one exists. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-43-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:44:**Format accessibility rules.** Four-option select renders every option as a\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-45-labelled button and never uses position as the only clue. True/false spells out\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-46-both values. Ordered pair labels first/second positions and supports reorder by\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-47-keyboard and touch. Typed answer announces validation requirements, preserves\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-72-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-73-For each card revision, reviewer `R1` (factual/rights editor) verifies every\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-74-assertion against the exact provenance locator, source permission and original\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:75:expression record. Reviewer `R2` (accessibility/copy editor), a different\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-76-person, verifies unambiguous language, answer options/aliases, explanation,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-77-screen-reader text, non-colour state wording, and localisation keys. R1's\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-78-accepted decision moves the record to `fact_checked`; R2's accepted decision\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-173-| Competition | No `competitionScopes` value appears on more than six cards: the declared maximums are FIFA World Cup 6, UEFA European Championship 3, Copa Am\u00e9rica 3, AFC Asian Cup 3, Premier League 6, LALIGA 4, Serie A 6, UEFA Champions League 6, and Ballon d'Or 2. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-174-| Club | No `clubIds` value appears on more than four cards: Liverpool, Barcelona, and AC Milan each appear four times; other cards have no club quota participant. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-175-| Eligibility | Every card is `published`, has all grammar fields, a resolvable provenance record with a checked date, no unresolved conflict, two distinct accepted reviews of its current revision, and no withdrawal. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md:176:| Originality/accessibility | Every card has accepted originality and accessibility/copy review findings, required text equivalents, and no player-facing copied/source text. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-177-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-178-The sample inventory intentionally remains `draft` until per-card research and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md-179-review are completed. Thus it is bounded and independently auditable now, while\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-10-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-11-`First Whistle` is a fixed five-card, non-timed onboarding round. It is\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-12-available from a new local profile when the installed tutorial package is\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:13:present, including offline. It does not need sign-in, a purchase, notifications,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-14-or a remote service. Each card has the indicated one purpose; its final\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-15-published wording, answer IDs, provenance, and two reviews are governed by the\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-16-question-card and adjudication bibles before it may ship.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-44-| `TUT-FX-04` | From TUT-04 submit its configured ordered pair, resolve, inspect explanation, continue. | `TUT-04 \u2192 TUT-05`; explanation availability is recorded; inspection does not change score, streak, or card position. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-45-| `TUT-FX-05` | Display TUT-05; `Pause`; restart; `Resume`; resolve; complete. | Pause snapshot has `activeCardId=TUT-05`, no unresolved answer, package `tutorial-v1`; restart restores that card; completion creates exactly one `first_whistle_complete` milestone and an immutable result. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-46-| `TUT-FX-06` | Repeat the completion command in TUT-FX-05 with the same completed-run ID and interaction ID. | Return the recorded completion/result; no second milestone, history entry, or score event is added. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:47:| `TUT-FX-07` | Start tutorial while offline with `tutorial-v1` cached; pause at TUT-05; restart while still offline. | Start, snapshot read, and resume succeed using cached package only; no network request is required. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-48-| `TUT-FX-08` | Start tutorial with no compatible cached tutorial package. | No run is created; show initial-content-required/retry/return-home state. It must not offer a substituted or partial tutorial. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-49-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-50-## GPI-009 \u2014 Mixed Fixture selection\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-87-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-88-## Optional timer and round lifecycle\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-89-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:90:Timer is an accessibility-neutral optional display mode: `off` is the default\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-91-and tutorial always forces `off`. Starting a standard round freezes the chosen\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-92-mode. `on` records elapsed active seconds only; it does not change selection,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-93-adjudication, score, streak, or availability. Pause, background interruption,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:94:and recovery stop elapsed time. A timeout can be emitted only for an explicitly\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-95-enabled timer according to the separately implemented GAME-007 scoring rule.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-96-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-97-| Transition | Preconditions | Required result |\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-104-| `feedback(last) \u2192 results` | Continue after final resolution. | Commit result once; reopening is idempotent. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-105-| `active or feedback \u2192 paused` | Explicit pause, background/interruption, or app shutdown at safe boundary. | Persist current safe snapshot; timer stops; no answer is inferred or submitted. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-106-| `paused \u2192 active or feedback` | Resume compatible confirmed snapshot. | Restore exact card, resolved-feedback state if any, selection and timer mode; content cannot switch mid-round. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:107:| `paused \u2192 recovery` | Draft corrupt/incompatible or write interrupted. | Preserve last confirmed snapshot and offer resume it, discard draft, or return home; never overwrite silently. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-108-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-109-### Lifecycle deterministic fixtures\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-110-\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-115-| `LIFE-FX-03` | Resolve card 1, then retry its submit command with same interaction ID. | One attempt/score event exists and active card is card 2 exactly once. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-116-| `LIFE-FX-04` | On active card 4, app backgrounds; process terminates; restart. | Restore the last confirmed active-card-4 snapshot with no inferred answer; timer remains stopped until resumed. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-117-| `LIFE-FX-05` | Resolve card 4, then storage write fails before promotion. | Keep prior confirmed snapshot, surface retry/continue-without-saving, and do not claim card 4 was saved. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:118:| `LIFE-FX-06` | A compatible package update arrives during an active `MF-1` run. | Current run continues on its frozen package; update stages for between rounds only. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-119-| `LIFE-FX-07` | Restart with corrupt draft but valid confirmed card-4 snapshot. | Quarantine draft and offer the confirmed snapshot or discard; do not silently start a different selection. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-120-| `LIFE-FX-08` | Complete and reopen a standard result with the same completed-run ID. | Return the stored result; no duplicate aggregate history, score, or milestone is created. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-121-| `LIFE-FX-09` | From home with compatible cached package, choose the `cup` theme and leave timer off. | Traverse `home \u2192 selecting_theme \u2192 ready`; ready state shows the deterministic `MIX-FX-05` IDs/count and its reuse disclosure before start. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-122-| `LIFE-FX-10` | Start the ready state in LIFE-FX-09. | Traverse `ready \u2192 active(card 1)` and commit frozen IDs/revisions, `MF-5`, selection seed, rule/package versions, and `timerMode=off`. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-123-| `LIFE-FX-11` | Resolve and continue cards 1\u20139 of LIFE-FX-01, then resolve and continue card 10. | Each of the first nine continuations traverses `feedback(card n) \u2192 active(card n+1)` after a safe save; the tenth traverses `feedback(last) \u2192 results` once. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-124-| `LIFE-FX-12` | Pause from feedback after resolving card 4, restart, and resume. | Traverse `feedback \u2192 paused \u2192 feedback`; card-4 feedback, explanation availability, and frozen selection are restored without a second attempt. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md:125:| `LIFE-FX-13` | Detect an incompatible/corrupt draft while paused and choose the recovery route. | Traverse `paused \u2192 recovery`; retain the confirmed snapshot and show resume-confirmed/discard-draft/return-home choices. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-126-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-127-## Accessibility and release boundary\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/round-lifecycle-bible.md-128-\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-94-| Current state | Permitted event / required evidence | Next state | Eligible |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-95-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-96-| `draft` | `submit_factual_check`: provenance, originality, accepted factual review | `fact_checked` | no |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:97:| `fact_checked` | `accept_accessibility_copy`: different reviewer, accepted revision review | `accessibility_edited` | no |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:98:| `accessibility_edited` | `accept_second_review`: distinct reviewer, grammar/alias validation | `second_reviewed` | no |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-99-| `second_reviewed` | `publish`: release editor, all release checks pass | `published` | yes |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-100-| pre-publication | `block`: dispute, missing rights, or validation failure | `blocked` | no |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-101-| `published` | `withdraw`: reason, effective UTC time, evidence | `withdrawn` | no |\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-108-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-109-A reported conflict blocks an unpublished card or withdraws a published card\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-110-immediately. Withdrawal records `factual_correction`, `source_rights`,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md:111:`ambiguity`, or `accessibility_defect`, effective time, evidence, and an\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-112-optional replacement. It does not silently replace cards or rewrite past rounds.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-113-New selection excludes it from that time; a presented attempt resolves against\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md-114-its presented revision. Only a corrected, newly reviewed revision may publish.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md-16-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md-17-## Output list\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md-18-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md:19:- `design-evidence/score-streak-and-results-bible.md`: score/streak rule table, 18 recovery/result fixtures, idempotent milestones, and text, non-colour, captioned/mute audio-equivalent feedback requirements.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md-20-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md-21-Do not create implementation code or B/R runbooks, and do not accept the manifest.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md-22-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md-23-## Acceptance criteria\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md-24-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0004.md:25:- Wrong, blank, timeout, and abandon remain recoverable and do not create duplicate completion.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-27-| GAME-001 | **Question-card grammar.** An original card has one unambiguous fact, prompt, format, category, era/competition tags, difficulty 1\u20133, answer rule, short explanation, and review/version state. Formats: four-option select, true/false, ordered pair, and short typed answer. | Ship only reviewed `published` cards. A card without provenance, answer rule, explanation, or two-editor approval is ineligible. Test: each sampled card adjudicates its canonical and configured accepted answers identically. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-28-| GAME-002 | **Catalogue batch A: \u201cKickoff Mix.\u201d** 48 original cards: 12 world tournament history, 12 domestic league moments, 12 club/manager/identity, 12 players/records. Each category has 4 cards at each band, max 6 cards per competition and no single club above 4. | Finite named release package: `QB-A-01` through `QB-A-48`, authored in four 12-card editorial batches. Exact facts, wording, sources, and rights clearance remain an editorial approval gate; placeholders never ship. Test: the manifest enforces totals, distributions, unique IDs, and no unpublished card. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-29-| GAME-003 | **Adjudication and provenance.** Select/true-false compare canonical IDs. Ordered pair compares ordered IDs. Typed answers normalise Unicode, case, punctuation, whitespace, diacritics, and configured aliases; it never uses fuzzy matching in release one. A rejected typed answer shows the canonical answer and explanation. | Each factual assertion links to a durable permitted source or approved internal research note, with checked date, reviewer, and correction history. Conflict or contested fact \u21d2 remove from eligibility until resolved. Test: alias, malformed, blank, ambiguous, and outdated-version cases have fixtures. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:30:| GAME-004 | **Freshness.** The repeat ledger records card ID and completion timestamp locally. A round excludes cards seen in its last two completed rounds where alternatives exist; if insufficient eligible cards exist, it discloses reuse rather than silently failing. | No renewable feed, scraping, or live refresh. Authoring flow: propose \u2192 source/provenance \u2192 factual check \u2192 accessibility/copy edit \u2192 second review \u2192 publish to a versioned batch \u2192 validate \u2192 release/rollback. Test: seeded selection is reproducible and respects the exclusion rule. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-31-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:32:**Visual/audio/accessibility:** cards use original broadcast-inspired category\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-33-colour families plus text labels/patterns; no colour alone encodes category or\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-34-result. Readable scalable typography, screen-reader labels, captions/text\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-35-equivalents for cues, and a reduced-motion feedback path are required. Original\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-45-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-46-| Unit | Design card / rule | First-release boundary and acceptance |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-47-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:48:| GAME-005 | **Round \u201cFirst Whistle.\u201d** Tutorial round contains 5 fixed, original tutorial cards (`TUT-01`\u2013`TUT-05`) covering selecting, typing, feedback, explanation, and pause/save. It is intentionally non-timed. | This is the complete first useful journey. Completion creates/updates local milestone `first_whistle_complete`; it cannot require account, network, purchase, or deferred content. Test: a new local profile can complete it offline and resume after app restart. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-49-| GAME-006 | **Round \u201cMixed Fixture.\u201d** A 10-card themed round draws from one selected category or the Kickoff Mix, with no more than two adjacent cards sharing format or difficulty. The player may pause; a displayed timer mode is optional and defaults off. | First release ships one tutorial and one configurable standard round template, no ranked/daily/live/event modes. Test: deterministic seed produces ten eligible cards and valid format alternation or records the shortage. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-50-| GAME-007 | **Scoring and streak.** Correct = 100 points; a consecutive-correct streak of 3+ adds 25 points to each later correct answer, capped at +100. Incorrect, timeout (only if enabled), blank submission, or abandon resets the active streak; score never decreases. Explanation is available after resolution. | No paid boosts, leaderboard, social comparison, or opaque difficulty multiplier. Test: table-driven sequence proves cap, reset, and per-attempt result; a retry is a new run, not an overwrite of history. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-51-| GAME-008 | **Result and return.** Results show answered/correct, score, best active-session streak, category, and next action: replay, choose theme, or exit. Progress is local milestones and aggregate history only, not RPG levels. | An interrupted run persists at a safe boundary before the next unresolved question. Completed result is idempotent: reopening cannot award twice. Test: complete/reopen, abandon/resume, corrupted draft, and delete-history paths are specified. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-52-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-53-**Dependencies:** GAME-005 needs published tutorial cards and persistence;\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-54-GAME-006 needs GAME-001\u2013004; GAME-007 consumes adjudication events; GAME-008\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:55:consumes score events and save/recovery. Visual family is bold category panels,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-56-neutral answer controls, and non-colour success/error indicators; audio is\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-57-supportive, optional, and captioned.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-58-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:59:### Accessible, recoverable multi-target experience \u2014 `GAME-009` to `GAME-012`\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-60-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:61:**Player outcome:** start, control, interrupt, recover, and return to a round\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-62-confidently on a supported surface. **Entities:** `LocalProfile`, `Settings`,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-63-`SaveSnapshot`, `RecoveryRecord`, `ContentVersion`, `ErrorNotice`,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-64-`InputAction`, `InstallState`, and `DiagnosticEvent`.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-65-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-66-| Unit | Design card / rule | First-release boundary and acceptance |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-67-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:68:| GAME-009 | **Guided start.** First launch offers an accessible plain-language tutorial entry, settings access, and a local profile without sign-in. Controls map select/navigate/confirm/back/pause to touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad. | No mandatory account. Permission denial for optional notifications/diagnostics changes no game path and explains how to alter it later. Test: every critical action is operable with keyboard and touch, focus is visible, and gamepad has an equivalent mapping. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:69:| GAME-010 | **Save/recovery.** Save immutable confirmed snapshots at tutorial completion, resolved question boundaries, explicit pause, and completed results. On failed write, retain the last confirmed snapshot and show retry/continue-without-saving. On corrupt draft, offer last confirmed snapshot or discard draft; never silently overwrite. | Remote sync/conflict requires approval and is excluded. Local deletion requires confirmation, names its effect, clears local profile/history/snapshots, and returns to first launch. Test: write failure, crash/restart, corrupt draft, and deletion fixtures preserve stated invariants. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:70:| GAME-011 | **Offline/update/error.** The installed content batch and current snapshot remain playable offline. A new content version is staged between rounds; an incompatible cache reports recovery steps and preserves confirmed save before cache reset. Unexpected errors show a plain-language retry/return-home path and optional minimised diagnostic consent. | No background live content requirement. Test: offline launch with cached assets, update mid-round, unavailable content, and diagnostic permission-denied behaviours are covered. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:71:| GAME-012 | **Platform adaptation.** Shared rule/content/save semantics on responsive web, PWA, Android, and iOS. Web adds pointer/keyboard/gamepad and responsive layouts; PWA adds install/offline cache/update UX; phones add touch targets and approved portrait/landscape choice. | No target-exclusive questions or rule differences. OS/browser matrix, orientation, performance, battery, thermal, size, store/privacy declarations, crash vendor, and exact language set remain approval gates. Test: capability matrix is exercised once targets are chosen. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-72-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-73-Accessibility applies to all three systems: text-size and contrast settings,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-74-reduced motion, captions/text equivalents, non-colour result encoding, focus\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-79-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-80-**Experience production package:** a finite first-release package contains the\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-81-five named tutorial cards, one settings/help copy set, input-action labels,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:82:result/recovery/empty-state strings, category visual tokens, and five original\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:83:optional cue families. Its workflow is interaction specification \u2192 accessible\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-84-copy/caption and focus review \u2192 original art/audio production \u2192 target\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:85:adaptation \u2192 keyboard/touch/gamepad and offline/recovery acceptance checks.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-86-It depends on the shared shell, settings, persistence, renderer, and target\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-87-adapters; it cannot depend on an account, remote service, or purchase.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-88-\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-92-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-93-| GAME-001\u2013004 | J1/J2/J4 (and J5 for versioned batch) | B content/adjudication; F delivery for batch lifecycle |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-94-| GAME-005\u2013008 | J1/J2/J3 | A shell/progress; C rules/score/feedback; D persistence for return |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:95:| GAME-009\u2013012 | J0/J1/J2/J3/J5 | D recovery, E accessibility/input/presentation, F delivery/targets |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-96-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-97-The machine-readable `implementation_map` in the companion JSON maps every\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-98-individual `GAME-*` unit, rather than treating this grouped table as a substitute.\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-3-sequence: 3\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-4-dependencies: GB0003,G0004\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-5-source_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md:6:source_catalogue_ids: GAME-009,GAME-010,GAME-011,GAME-012,GPI-012,GPI-013,GPI-014,GPI-015\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md:7:title: Define accessible recovery and target parity bible\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-8-browser_impact: not_applicable\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-9-playwright_spec:\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-10-design_authoring_batch: GB0003\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-12-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-13-## Objective\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-14-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md:15:Write accepted evidence for GAME-009\u2013012/GPI-012\u2013015: four input mappings, captions/contrast/text/motion equivalents, four recovery states, offline/update notices, and web/PWA/Android/iOS parity and certification matrix.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-16-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-17-## Output list\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-18-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md:19:- `design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md`: four input mappings, accessible feedback equivalents, recovery/offline/update states, and web/PWA/Android/iOS rule/content/save parity matrix.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-20-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-21-Do not create target-exclusive content, mandatory accounts/sync, code, B/R runbooks, or manifest acceptance.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md-22-\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md-27-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md-28-## Visual and audio intent\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md-29-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md:30:Visual direction: original modern football-broadcast graphics, bold accessible\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md-31-category colours, large score numerals, readable typography, disciplined card\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md-32-geometry, clear answer states, and restrained motion. Prompt hierarchy comes\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md-33-first, answer action second, score/streak third. Colour is never the only cue;\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '59,90p' projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md\nsed -n '25,75p' projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsed -n '1,120p' projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/GB0003.md\nsed -n '1,100p' projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n### Accessible, recoverable multi-target experience \u2014 `GAME-009` to `GAME-012`\n\n**Player outcome:** start, control, interrupt, recover, and return to a round\nconfidently on a supported surface. **Entities:** `LocalProfile`, `Settings`,\n`SaveSnapshot`, `RecoveryRecord`, `ContentVersion`, `ErrorNotice`,\n`InputAction`, `InstallState`, and `DiagnosticEvent`.\n\n| Unit | Design card / rule | First-release boundary and acceptance |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GAME-009 | **Guided start.** First launch offers an accessible plain-language tutorial entry, settings access, and a local profile without sign-in. Controls map select/navigate/confirm/back/pause to touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad. | No mandatory account. Permission denial for optional notifications/diagnostics changes no game path and explains how to alter it later. Test: every critical action is operable with keyboard and touch, focus is visible, and gamepad has an equivalent mapping. |\n| GAME-010 | **Save/recovery.** Save immutable confirmed snapshots at tutorial completion, resolved question boundaries, explicit pause, and completed results. On failed write, retain the last confirmed snapshot and show retry/continue-without-saving. On corrupt draft, offer last confirmed snapshot or discard draft; never silently overwrite. | Remote sync/conflict requires approval and is excluded. Local deletion requires confirmation, names its effect, clears local profile/history/snapshots, and returns to first launch. Test: write failure, crash/restart, corrupt draft, and deletion fixtures preserve stated invariants. |\n| GAME-011 | **Offline/update/error.** The installed content batch and current snapshot remain playable offline. A new content version is staged between rounds; an incompatible cache reports recovery steps and preserves confirmed save before cache reset. Unexpected errors show a plain-language retry/return-home path and optional minimised diagnostic consent. | No background live content requirement. Test: offline launch with cached assets, update mid-round, unavailable content, and diagnostic permission-denied behaviours are covered. |\n| GAME-012 | **Platform adaptation.** Shared rule/content/save semantics on responsive web, PWA, Android, and iOS. Web adds pointer/keyboard/gamepad and responsive layouts; PWA adds install/offline cache/update UX; phones add touch targets and approved portrait/landscape choice. | No target-exclusive questions or rule differences. OS/browser matrix, orientation, performance, battery, thermal, size, store/privacy declarations, crash vendor, and exact language set remain approval gates. Test: capability matrix is exercised once targets are chosen. |\n\nAccessibility applies to all three systems: text-size and contrast settings,\nreduced motion, captions/text equivalents, non-colour result encoding, focus\norder, semantic labels, sufficient touch targets, and no time limit by default.\nLocalisation inputs are externalised prompt, answer, explanation, category, and\nUI strings; only a future approved language may add translated content after\nanswer aliases and factual review are validated.\n\n**Experience production package:** a finite first-release package contains the\nfive named tutorial cards, one settings/help copy set, input-action labels,\nresult/recovery/empty-state strings, category visual tokens, and five original\noptional cue families. Its workflow is interaction specification \u2192 accessible\ncopy/caption and focus review \u2192 original art/audio production \u2192 target\nadaptation \u2192 keyboard/touch/gamepad and offline/recovery acceptance checks.\nIt depends on the shared shell, settings, persistence, renderer, and target\nadapters; it cannot depend on an account, remote service, or purchase.\n\n## Journey and implementation-domain crosswalk\n\nnon-taunting feedback. Authors avoid stereotypes, unreviewed claims, and\nimitation of reference publications.\n\n## Visual and audio intent\n\nVisual direction: original modern football-broadcast graphics, bold accessible\ncategory colours, large score numerals, readable typography, disciplined card\ngeometry, clear answer states, and restrained motion. Prompt hierarchy comes\nfirst, answer action second, score/streak third. Colour is never the only cue;\nthe system supports adjustable text, focus, reduced motion, high contrast,\ncaptions, and responsive portrait-first layouts. Use original abstract pitch\nlines, stat blocks, signal sweeps, and celebration shapes\u2014never real club,\ncompetition, broadcaster, publisher, or QuizUp marks, kit designs, screenshots,\nor screen composition.\n\nAudio direction: an original restrained percussive entry bed; distinct correct,\nincorrect, streak, optional urgency, and completion cues; and a warm short\nresults sting. Bright electronic percussion, claps, soft brass-like synth\naccents, and abstract crowd energy are allowed; sampled or imitated chants,\nanthems, broadcasts, clubs, or games are not. Essential meaning always has\ntext/visual alternatives plus volume, mute, and caption/description options.\nExact cue quantities/durations/loop policy remain production decisions.\n\nThe Athletic and QuizUp are functional references only: no copying of branding,\nquestions, wording, copy, art, audio, layouts, flow choreography, or distinctive\ninteractions. All expression is independently authored.\n---\ntask_id: GB0003\nsequence: 2\ndependencies: GD0001\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/02-game-design-bible.json,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-009,GAME-010,GAME-011,GAME-012,GPI-012,GPI-013,GPI-014,GPI-015\ntitle: Author accessibility and target design runbook\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nCreate only G0005 for GAME-009\u2013012 and GPI-012\u2013015: equivalent controls and feedback, recovery, offline/update messaging, and target parity/certification evidence.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `G0005.md` only; it must declare `design_authoring_batch: GB0003` and create/review `design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md`.\n\nDo not create code, B/R runbooks, target-exclusive rules, mandatory accounts, remote sync, or final audit.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- No more than five G tasks are created and it declares `design_authoring_batch: GB0003`.\n---\ntask_id: G0005\nsequence: 3\ndependencies: GB0003,G0004\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-009,GAME-010,GAME-011,GAME-012,GPI-012,GPI-013,GPI-014,GPI-015\ntitle: Define accessible recovery and target parity bible\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\ndesign_authoring_batch: GB0003\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite accepted evidence for GAME-009\u2013012/GPI-012\u2013015: four input mappings, captions/contrast/text/motion equivalents, four recovery states, offline/update notices, and web/PWA/Android/iOS parity and certification matrix.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md`: four input mappings, accessible feedback equivalents, recovery/offline/update states, and web/PWA/Android/iOS rule/content/save parity matrix.\n\nDo not create target-exclusive content, mandatory accounts/sync, code, B/R runbooks, or manifest acceptance.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Each meaning has a non-audio, non-colour equivalent and target adaptations cannot alter shared rules or saves.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 2 'GPI-012|GPI-013|GPI-014|GPI-015' projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.json projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-feature-model.md projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md-17-| GAME-007 | GPI-010: rule table, 12 edge fixtures | GPI-006, 009 | Rules + accessibility | Score/streak equivalent-feedback tests |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md-18-| GAME-008 | GPI-011: result and milestone states | GPI-009\u2013010, 014 | Design + UI | Idempotence/recovery lifecycle tests |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md:19:| GAME-009 | GPI-012: profile/settings plus four input maps | \u2014 | Accessibility + platform | Input and accessibility review |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md:20:| GAME-010 | GPI-013: four recovery states, eight faults | GPI-011 | Persistence + accessibility | Fault-injection recovery tests |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md:21:| GAME-011 | GPI-014: cache/update notices and six fixtures | GPI-002\u2013005, 013 | Release + platform | Offline/update/error tests |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md:22:| GAME-012 | GPI-015: four-target parity/certification matrix | GPI-012\u2013014 | Platform + release | Target evidence and certification checklist |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md-23-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md-24-The machine-readable [inventory](game-production-inventory.json) is\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The project already defines the underlying game and recovery invariants. I found the requested output is a new design-evidence bible, so I\u2019m adding it without changing implementation scope.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/game-design-runbooks/G0005.md\"],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"Reviewed task and source specifications.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: documentation-only design evidence.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cd91020b91c557225c3741331cf577b12400966c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@\n+# Accessibility, recovery, and target parity bible\n+\n+## Purpose and non-negotiable invariants\n+\n+This is the accepted design evidence for `GAME-009`\u2013`GAME-012` and\n+`GPI-012`\u2013`GPI-015`. It governs the shared first-release game on responsive\n+web, PWA, Android, and iOS. It does not approve an account, remote sync,\n+target-exclusive content, a target-exclusive ruleset, or a target delivery\n+matrix.\n+\n+Every target consumes the same published question revision, adjudication rule,\n+score-event ledger, local-profile schema, confirmed-snapshot format, and\n+result/milestone idempotency rule. An adapter may translate input, layout,\n+installation, permission wording, or cache handling; it must not transform an\n+answer, scoring outcome, round seed, content eligibility decision, or confirmed\n+save. A target that cannot read a supported confirmed snapshot must preserve it\n+and enter recovery; it must never replace it with an empty profile.\n+\n+Essential meaning is always exposed in plain visible text and semantic state.\n+Audio, colour, iconography, vibration, and animation may reinforce that meaning\n+but are never its sole carrier. The normal round has no time limit; optional\n+timer mode remains explicitly enabled and its availability does not alter the\n+following equivalence requirements.\n+\n+## GPI-012 \u2014 profile, settings, and four input mappings\n+\n+First launch creates a local profile without sign-in and presents **Start First\n+Whistle** and **Settings** as plain-language controls. Optional notification and\n+diagnostic permission denial leaves the same tutorial, settings, saving, and\n+return paths available. Settings include text-size, high-contrast presentation,\n+reduced motion, cue volume/mute, captions/descriptions, and input help.\n+\n+| Shared action | Touch | Pointer | Keyboard | Gamepad |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Navigate / choose a control | Tap its labelled target; swipe only scrolls, never chooses. | Click its labelled target; wheel only scrolls. | Tab / Shift+Tab moves focus; arrow keys move within an answer group or ordered pair. | D-pad or left stick moves focus; no hover-only state is required. |\n+| Select an answer / reorder | Tap option; drag is optional and has visible move up/down alternatives. | Click option; drag is optional and has visible move up/down alternatives. | Space or Enter selects; ordered pair uses documented arrow-key move commands. | South button selects; ordered pair exposes labelled move commands using D-pad. |\n+| Confirm / continue | Tap **Submit**, **Continue**, or the named recovery action. | Click the same labelled control. | Enter or Space activates the focused named control. | South button activates the focused named control. |\n+| Back / pause / open help | Tap visible **Back**, **Pause**, or **Help**; system back is an equivalent where available. | Click the visible named control. | Escape returns/backtracks where safe; P pauses; both are documented and focus remains visible. | East button returns/backtracks where safe; Menu/Start pauses; both are documented. |\n+\n+No action depends on a gesture, hover, pointer precision, or platform system\n+button alone. Back never discards an unresolved answer, a draft, or local data:\n+it reaches the existing pause, confirmation, or recovery path. Focus order is\n+prompt \u2192 instructions \u2192 answer controls \u2192 submit \u2192 explanation/secondary\n+actions, with a persistent visible focus indicator; feedback moves focus to its\n+heading once and does not steal it for animation.\n+\n+## Accessible feedback equivalents\n+\n+The following table is the release copy and presentation contract. Screen-reader\n+announcement is the stated text once per state change; captions/descriptions\n+show the same essential message. Contrast mode preserves the text and semantic\n+state rather than replacing it with a colour-only palette.\n+\n+| Meaning | Required visible and semantic text | Non-colour equivalent | Audio/caption equivalent | Reduced-motion path |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Category / question context | Category name and question number (for example, \u201cWorld tournament history \u2014 Question 3 of 10\u201d). | Named category plus a distinct pattern/label; never colour alone. | No cue is required; any entry cue caption repeats the category/context. | Static panel and label; no sweep required. |\n+| Selected, unselected, and disabled answer | \u201cSelected: [answer]\u201d, \u201cNot selected\u201d, or \u201cUnavailable until [condition]\u201d. | Border, check/selection icon with accessible name, and text state. | No cue is required; any selection cue is captioned \u201cAnswer selected\u201d. | Static state change. |\n+| Correct, incorrect, blank, or enabled-timer timeout | Outcome name, points, streak result, canonical answer/explanation, and next action. | Labelled success/error/empty/time icon or pattern, not green/red alone. | Caption names the same outcome and score/streak information; mute changes no meaning. | Static feedback with no forced celebration, shake, flash, or countdown motion. |\n+| Streak / score update | \u201cScore: N. Streak: N.\u201d and, when applicable, bonus/cap text. | Labelled streak marker and numeral; not a colour, pulse, or sound alone. | Caption names points, streak, bonus, or cap. | Static score/streak marker. |\n+| Pause, saved, or recovery condition | State heading, what is retained, any risk, and named actions. | Icon/pattern is supplementary to the heading and action labels. | Caption/description repeats heading and named actions; no cue is required. | No auto-moving modal or animated warning. |\n+| Offline, update, unavailable content, or unexpected error | Plain-language notice naming availability, retained progress, and next action. | Text heading and icon/pattern; status is not conveyed through network colour alone. | If a cue plays, caption repeats the notice; mute changes no path. | Static notice; no looping spinner as the only status. |\n+\n+All minimum target contrast, text scaling, semantic-label, and touch-target\n+requirements are subject to the selected OS/browser matrix. Until that matrix is\n+approved, certification records the actual settings and assistive technology\n+used rather than claiming a numeric platform conformance level.\n+\n+## GPI-013 \u2014 recovery states and fault evidence\n+\n+`SaveSnapshot` means an immutable confirmed snapshot. A draft is never a\n+confirmed save. At tutorial completion, each resolved-question boundary,\n+explicit pause, and completed result, the system attempts to write a new\n+confirmed snapshot without mutating the previous one.\n+\n+| Recovery state | Entry condition | Required notice and actions | Preservation invariant |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `write_failed` | A confirmed-snapshot write fails. | \u201cProgress could not be saved. Your last confirmed progress is safe.\u201d Offer **Retry** and **Continue without saving**. | Retain and make recoverable the previous confirmed snapshot; do not imply that the current unresolved state is saved. |\n+| `interrupted_resume` | App/browser/OS ends or backgrounds after a prior confirmed boundary. | \u201cContinue your saved round?\u201d Offer **Resume confirmed round** and **Return home**. | Restore the exact confirmed content revision, position, score ledger, and unresolved state; interruption creates no blank, timeout, abandon, or duplicate completion event. |\n+| `draft_recovery` | Draft is corrupt, incomplete, or incompatible while a confirmed snapshot exists. | \u201cA recent in-progress change could not be recovered. Your confirmed progress is safe.\u201d Offer **Resume confirmed progress**, **Discard draft**, and **Return home**. | Keep the confirmed snapshot until the player explicitly deletes local data; never silently overwrite it with the draft or a new profile. |\n+| `delete_local_data` | Player requests local-data deletion. | Confirmation names that local profile, history, results, and snapshots will be removed and cannot be resumed. Offer **Delete local data** and **Cancel**. | Only confirmed deletion clears those local records and returns to first launch. Cancel changes nothing; remote state is not implied. |\n+\n+Fault-injection evidence must cover: failed write at a resolved boundary;\n+failed pause write; termination after confirmed pause; termination after a\n+resolved attempt; corrupt draft with a valid snapshot; incompatible draft with a\n+valid snapshot; retry succeeding after `write_failed`; and cancellation versus\n+confirmation of local deletion. Each fixture asserts unchanged shared rules,\n+no silent loss of confirmed progress, and no duplicated result/milestone.\n+\n+## GPI-014 \u2014 offline, update, and error notices\n+\n+The installed published content batch and current confirmed snapshot support a\n+basic session offline. No notice may block a locally available tutorial or\n+round merely because a network, optional permission, or diagnostic endpoint is\n+unavailable.\n+\n+| Notice ID | Trigger | Player-facing notice | Required handling |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `OFFLINE-CACHED` | Network is unavailable and required installed content is present. | \u201cYou\u2019re offline. Installed questions and saved progress are available.\u201d | Start/resume remains available; suppress live-refresh expectation. |\n+| `OFFLINE-CONTENT-UNAVAILABLE` | Requested content is not installed and cannot be fetched. | \u201cThis question set is not available offline. Try again when connected or choose an installed round.\u201d | Preserve current confirmed save; offer installed content or return home. |\n+| `UPDATE-STAGED` | A compatible content version is available during a round. | \u201cAn update is ready and will be used after this round.\u201d | Freeze the active round\u2019s content revision and rules; apply only between rounds. |\n+| `CACHE-INCOMPATIBLE` | Cache cannot support the pending content version. | \u201cAn update needs a cache refresh. Your confirmed progress will be kept.\u201d | Preserve/export the confirmed snapshot before reset; provide **Refresh cache** and **Return home**. |\n+| `UNEXPECTED-ERROR` | A non-recoverable unexpected operation error occurs. | \u201cSomething went wrong. Your confirmed progress is safe.\u201d | Offer **Retry** and **Return home**; optional minimised diagnostic consent is separate and denial changes no recovery route. |\n+\n+Six release fixtures are required: offline launch of First Whistle with cached\n+assets; offline resume from a confirmed snapshot; unavailable non-installed\n+content; compatible update arriving mid-round; incompatible-cache refresh with\n+confirmed-save restoration; and unexpected error with diagnostic permission\n+denied. Each verifies the exact notice, named action, preserved snapshot, and\n+unchanged adjudication/score semantics.\n+\n+## GPI-015 \u2014 target parity and certification matrix\n+\n+The matrix states first-release parity requirements, not approval of a specific\n+device, browser, orientation, performance budget, packaging route, store\n+submission, crash provider, privacy declaration, or language set. Those remain\n+human approval gates. \u201cRequired\u201d means a candidate target must demonstrate the\n+item before it can be certified in the eventual selected matrix.\n+\n+| Capability / certification evidence | Responsive web | PWA | Android phone | iPhone (iOS) |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Shared content, answer, score, save, recovery, result, and milestone semantics | Required; no web rule branch. | Required; no PWA rule branch. | Required; no Android rule branch. | Required; no iOS rule branch. |\n+| Input and focus evidence | Keyboard, pointer, touch, and gamepad maps; responsive visible focus. | Browser/device-supported maps plus install-surface focus evidence. | Touch map and external keyboard where OS/device offers it; visible focus for non-touch navigation. | Touch map and external keyboard where OS/device offers it; visible focus for non-touch navigation. |\n+| Accessible feedback evidence | Text scale, contrast, captions/descriptions, non-colour states, reduced motion, semantic labels. | Same shared feedback contract before/after install and offline. | Same shared feedback contract using selected OS accessibility settings. | Same shared feedback contract using selected OS accessibility settings. |\n+| Offline/update evidence | Cached installed content/snapshot and notices where web delivery supports them. | Install, offline cache, staged update, and incompatible-cache recovery notices. | Packaged installed content, offline snapshot, staged update/recovery notices. | Packaged installed content, offline snapshot, staged update/recovery notices. |\n+| Form-factor adaptation | Responsive phone, tablet, and desktop layout; no hidden critical control. | Responsive installed layout; no PWA-only content/mode. | Sufficient touch targets; orientation only after approval. | Sufficient touch targets; orientation only after approval. |\n+| Certification record | Chosen browser/OS/device, input methods, assistive-tech/settings evidence, fixture IDs, defects, and sign-off. | Above plus install/offline/update evidence. | Chosen device/OS, packaging/store/privacy evidence, battery/thermal/size budget evidence, and sign-off. | Chosen device/OS, packaging/store/privacy evidence, battery/thermal/size budget evidence, and sign-off. |\n+\n+Certification is blocked, rather than waived, until the target matrix and its\n+approval gates are selected. A failure on any target is resolved by fixing the\n+shared core or its adapter; it cannot be resolved by altering a question,\n+answer rule, score rule, save schema, or recovery guarantee for that target.\n+\n+## Release evidence checklist\n+\n+- Record one successful keyboard-and-touch traversal of every critical action,\n+  plus the gamepad equivalent on supported web/browser candidates.\n+- Verify each feedback-table meaning with cue volume muted, high contrast,\n+  enlarged text, captions/descriptions enabled, and reduced motion enabled.\n+- Execute all eight GPI-013 fault fixtures and six GPI-014 offline/update/error\n+  fixtures against each selected target\u2019s applicable capabilities.\n+- Compare serialized confirmed snapshots and resulting score/milestone records\n+  across targets for the same round seed and input sequence.\n+- Retain the selected target/device/browser/OS evidence and approval record;\n+  no unselected target is represented as certified.\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/design-evidence/accessibility-recovery-and-target-parity-bible.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0